# Bentley Continental GT second generation, 2011-2018.
#
# The 2011 car: the sharper, more sculpted body with the more upright
# matrix grille, the LED headlamps and the 6.0 W12. UK deliveries from the
# first quarter of 2011; replaced in May 2018.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bentley_Continental_GT
#
# Dimensions 4.806 x 1.944 x 1.404 m, wheelbase 2.746 m (Wikipedia infobox;
# Bentley's own 2011 specification sheet was not retrieved, so these are
# grade (c) and are recorded as unconfirmed).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level profile, square to the flank at
# wheel-arch height.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the 17 standard colours of Bentley's "The New
# Continental GT Range" brochure: Beluga, Glacier White, Dark Sapphire and
# St. James' Red are among them. Weights 20, 16, 12, 10, total 58, provisional.
#
# Speed 318 km/h. Comfort 155/563, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 155. Classes 3,4.
# Dates: intro January 2011; retires staggered 2026-2029 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bentley-continental-gt-2.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bentley-continental-gt-2.dae. References:
# citycars/references/bentley-continental-gt-2/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the W12 coupe is modelled. The grille mesh, the lamp
# rings, the boot recess and the wheel detail are simplified, and chrome is
# limited to trim so that the car does not render as a white block at pak
# scale.


obj=citycar
